---
description: Chain-of-Verification for analysis and planning (internal CoVe)
alwaysApply: true
---

# CoVe policy (Chain of Verification)

Apply when you analyze or decide next plan/steps - not for trivial read-only Q&A.

## Procedure (internal - do not expose steps to user)

1. Draft answer/plan
2. Write 3-5 verification questions (fewer for trivial tasks)
3. Answer each independently using evidence (repo, memory, web, logs, tests)
4. Revise final output

## Complexity and impact rubric

- Complexity: C0 single step | C1 subtasks | C2 story | C3 epic
- Impact: I0 minor | I1 moderate | I2 breaking | I3 critical

Max CoVe iterations (hard cap; stop early if uncertainty gone):

| Scope | Max iterations |
|-------|----------------|
| C0 AND I0 | 1 |
| C1 OR I1 | 2 |
| C2 OR I2 | 3 |
| C3 OR I3 | 4 |
| C3 AND I3 | 5 |

## Output footer

- Non-trivial (C1+ or I1+): CoVe: zastosowano (N pytan weryfikacyjnych).
- Trivial (C0 I0): CoVe pominięte (C0 I0).

CoVe validates plans whether from Plan Mode or Shrimp.
